---
title: "Using stdlib.semver"
author: bad-antics
date: 2026-11-28
abstract: Parse, compare, validate, and bump Semantic Versioning strings with the Lateralus standard library.

# Parse a version

Import `semver` and parse a version into a five-item list: major, minor, patch, pre-release, and build metadata.

```ltl
import semver

let v = semver.parse("v1.4.0-beta.2+build.19")
println(semver.major(v))
println(semver.prerelease(v))
println(semver.build_meta(v))
```

The optional leading `v` is accepted. `to_string` formats a parsed value again, while `format` and `format_full` build versions from components.

# Compare releases

Use `lt`, `gt`, `lte`, `gte`, and `eq` instead of comparing version strings directly. A stable release has higher precedence than its pre-release, and build metadata does not affect precedence.

```ltl
let candidate = semver.parse("1.4.0-rc.1")
let release = semver.parse("1.4.0")
if semver.lt(candidate, release) {
    println("release the candidate first")
}
```

The pinned vectors in `tests/stdlib_semver.ltl` cover the ordering from the SemVer 2.0.0 specification, including numeric and dotted pre-release identifiers.

# Bump and constrain

`bump_major`, `bump_minor`, and `bump_patch` return stable versions and clear pre-release/build metadata. `satisfies_caret` checks a compatible major/minor range, while `satisfies_tilde` checks a patch-level range.

```ltl
let version = semver.parse("1.4.2")
let next = semver.bump_patch(version)
println(semver.to_string(next))       // 1.4.3
println(semver.satisfies_caret(version, 1, 3)) // true
println(semver.satisfies_tilde(version, 1, 4)) // true
```

Run the companion program with `lateralus run examples/semver_demo.ltl`.
